            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, no, that is too much customization for what seems to be quite common interface.\r\n\r\nTo be clear:\r\n- This message is not for change confirmation, but when you exit 'mini.files' (by default with `q`) when there is at least one modified buffer (meaning there are changes and after pressing `y` they will be forgotten). To confirm changes, press `=` (by default).\r\n- The default choice is marked with `[]` brackets. So you don't have to press `Y` to close it without synchronization, `<CR>` (`<Enter>`) also works.\r\n- It shouldn't be capital `Y` and `N`. Lower case `y` and `n` works too.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, no, that is too much customization for what seems to be quite common interface.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To be clear:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>This message is not for change confirmation, but when you exit 'mini.files' (by default with <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code>) when there is at least one modified buffer (meaning there are changes and after pressing <code class=\"notranslate\">y</code> they will be forgotten). To confirm changes, press <code class=\"notranslate\">=</code> (by default).</li>\n<li>The default choice is marked with <code class=\"notranslate\">[]</code> brackets. So you don't have to press <code class=\"notranslate\">Y</code> to close it without synchronization, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;CR&gt;</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Enter&gt;</code>) also works.</li>\n<li>It shouldn't be capital <code class=\"notranslate\">Y</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">N</code>. Lower case <code class=\"notranslate\">y</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">n</code> works too.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry, no, that is too much customization for what seems to be quite common interface.\nTo be clear:\n\nThis message is not for change confirmation, but when you exit 'mini.files' (by default with q) when there is at least one modified buffer (meaning there are changes and after pressing y they will be forgotten). To confirm changes, press = (by default).\nThe default choice is marked with [] brackets. So you don't have to press Y to close it without synchronization, <CR> (<Enter>) also works.\nIt shouldn't be capital Y and N. Lower case y and n works too.",
